Hi Phillip,

You can save the screen output of a particular man page
using standard shell redirection, for example:

	# man cc > cc.txt

This will preserve any formatting (e.g. bolding, underlines, etc)
in the original output, but it does leave you a copy that you
can 'more' directly, or print out.

Man page source files are in nroff format, so you could
also process the file directly if you so desired.  See
the catman(8) man page for some hints and tips...and good luck!

Dan



