>nroff -man /usr/man/manX/blah.X

If the chap wants something printable on a generic line printer, he might also
want to pipe the output through col -b.  If he wants to do things manually, he
can pipe the output of nroff, but he can also let the man program take care of
the details.  For example,
man ls | col -b > ls.out
would get him a plain copy of the ls man page.  However, people usually want to
do this to print man pages so he can go direct to print with
man ls | col -b | lpr
